code_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933604#post933604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a guy in my old LARP group who claimed to be an actual witch. It was also quite clear that he learned everything he knew about witches from watching Charmed.<br /> <br /> I didn't really have a point there, just felt like sharing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stories like this are pretty much what I live for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T22:49:06-07:00","id":933739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933588#post933588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: Yes, it's <i>immediately</i> obvious that Mages, as written, fit. However, a random guy off the street is... unlikely to use that definition for Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Apparently there was once a thread on the Stormfront forums where a bunch of white supremicists tried to come up for a justification for liking Drizzt.<br /> <br /> Forgive me if I don't go looking for a precise <i>link</i> for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;People that do magic.&quot; slots in. The rest is flavour to your leisure. Your question feels a little obtuse, particularly because it simultaneously uses preconceptions to try to justify itself as an argument......against preconceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T23:02:18-07:00","id":933746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933535#post933535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that a continuation of branding had a lot to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that a continuation of branding had <i>everything</i> to do with it. Well\u2026 that, and \u201cmage\u201d covers more ground than \u201cwitch\u201d does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T23:04:56-07:00","id":933749,"title":"","content":"OP made a good point about wizards not being a horror archetype, and it's one of the main things that always bugged me about ChroD, one of the few things in one of my favorite settings that just didn't fit. <br /> <br /> To me, every gameline should be about putting the players in the role of a kind of archetypal monster (bonus if it's one of the classic Universal monsters), and Mage just doesn't do that. Mages aren't like the magic users that appear in horror stories and horror movies- when magic use comes up, it's often on a level best represented by a lesser template. <br /> <br /> You know what monster does cover the themes of hubris and forbidden knowledge that Mage claims to cover? It's without a doubt one of the most popular kinds of monster to ever enter pop culture. They've been the villains of more horror movies than mages, werewolves, and mummies PUT TOGETHER. They're undeniably monstrous yet still enviable and often oddly relatable. It's a monster with almost infinite potential for players and storytelling. A monster that would fill mage's niche far better than Mage does. But this monster exists only as minor template and backstory oddities and has no line of its own. What monster am I talking about? <br /> <br /> The mad scientist. One of the single most popular archetypes of horror fiction. Mad scientists literally shaped the genre and have Universal pedigree. Frankenstein's monster got his own line, but the doctor himself spawned his own lineage of monsters. Dr. Moreau, Doctor Doom, Dr. Rotwang, Dr. Venture, countless others. <br /> <br /> The mad scientist and the galvanic chimera are my favorite &quot;classic monsters&quot;, and that's why I loved Genius and Ascension and was disappointed with Promethean and Mage. It's what drove me to start my Mage: The Transgression project, which I think you'd find interesting: I'm remaking Awakening, trying to turn it into a streamlined blend of the best things about Ascension and Genius that truly emphasizes the idea of mages as monsters and pushes the connection to classic horror. And yes, there's a lot of mad science. <br /> <br /> Also, to me, a gnostic occultist dealing with dark mysteries in a setting designed to evoke and explore the themes of classic (especially Universal and pulp) horror shouldn't be a superhero with reality-warping magical might, they should be someone with very limited magical skill won at great cost, every ritual and spell a great effort. If you want to be someone who can light people on fire or move stuff with your mind, be a psychic. Out of control espers are much more of a horror thing that mages. That's why I'm so excited for Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T00:03:04-07:00","id":933761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933749#post933749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, every gameline should be about putting the players in the role of a kind of archetypal monster (bonus if it's one of the classic Universal monsters), and Mage just doesn't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much none of them do that apart from maybe vampire. Aside from Hunter, CofD has never been about creating archetypal monsters, it's always been about creating their own unique spin on something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933604#post933604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a guy in my old LARP group who claimed to be an actual witch. It was also quite clear that he learned everything he knew about witches from watching Charmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, same here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T00:05:07-07:00","id":933763,"title":"","content":"If your contention is that mages aren't a horror archetype, then I'd recommend against calling your homebrew horror archetype \u201cMage\u201d. Just call them Geniuses, and note that many of the so-called mystical arts were at one point or another considered to be sciences: alchemy and feng shui, to name two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T02:17:06-07:00","id":933787,"title":"","content":"If wizards aren't part of the standard monsters of the horror genre... I'm pretty sure that makes Clive Barker sad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T08:39:23-07:00","id":933912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933761#post933761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, same here.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was also a guy named Michael... You're not from Washington state, are you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T09:23:00-07:00","id":933934,"title":"","content":"Wielders of occult powers have been monsters and villains since time immemorial. Whether it's Hansel and Gretel or The Craft, from practitioners of Mangkukulam in the Phillipenes to the yee naaldlooshii among the Navajo, the occultists and practitioners have often been the villains. Even the &quot;white mages&quot; in the world are alien, mysterious, and debateably untrustworthy, driven by forces the average man does not comprehend.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no, mages are terrifying monsters, and they belong in the pantheon of modern pulp horror. THe fact we have Potter and Dresden softening the matter is not much counter-persuasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T09:51:28-07:00","id":933948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933934#post933934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wielders of occult powers have been monsters and villains since time immemorial. Whether it's Hansel and Gretel or The Craft, from practitioners of Mangkukulam in the Phillipenes to the yee naaldlooshii among the Navajo, the occultists and practitioners have often been the villains. Even the &amp;quot;white mages&amp;quot; in the world are alien, mysterious, and debateably untrustworthy, driven by forces the average man does not comprehend.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no, mages are terrifying monsters, and they belong in the pantheon of modern pulp horror. THe fact we have Potter and Dresden softening the matter is not much counter-persuasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that Mages in ChroD resemble Potter and Dresden much more than they resemble the examples of monsters that you gave. Also, Hansel and Gretel is Changeling's turf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T10:09:42-07:00","id":933958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933749#post933749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP made a good point about wizards not being a horror archetype, and it's one of the main things that always bugged me about ChroD, one of the few things in one of my favorite settings that just didn't fit. <br /> <br /> To me, every gameline should be about putting the players in the role of a kind of archetypal monster (bonus if it's one of the classic Universal monsters), and Mage just doesn't do that. Mages aren't like the magic users that appear in horror stories and horror movies- when magic use comes up, it's often on a level best represented by a lesser template. <br /> <br /> You know what monster does cover the themes of hubris and forbidden knowledge that Mage claims to cover? It's without a doubt one of the most popular kinds of monster to ever enter pop culture. They've been the villains of more horror movies than mages, werewolves, and mummies PUT TOGETHER. They're undeniably monstrous yet still enviable and often oddly relatable. It's a monster with almost infinite potential for players and storytelling. A monster that would fill mage's niche far better than Mage does. But this monster exists only as minor template and backstory oddities and has no line of its own. What monster am I talking about? <br /> <br /> The mad scientist. One of the single most popular archetypes of horror fiction. Mad scientists literally shaped the genre and have Universal pedigree. Frankenstein's monster got his own line, but the doctor himself spawned his own lineage of monsters. Dr. Moreau, Doctor Doom, Dr. Rotwang, Dr. Venture, countless others. <br /> <br /> The mad scientist and the galvanic chimera are my favorite &amp;quot;classic monsters&amp;quot;, and that's why I loved Genius and Ascension and was disappointed with Promethean and Mage. It's what drove me to start my Mage: The Transgression project, which I think you'd find interesting: I'm remaking Awakening, trying to turn it into a streamlined blend of the best things about Ascension and Genius that truly emphasizes the idea of mages as monsters and pushes the connection to classic horror. And yes, there's a lot of mad science. <br /> <br /> Also, to me, a gnostic occultist dealing with dark mysteries in a setting designed to evoke and explore the themes of classic (especially Universal and pulp) horror shouldn't be a superhero with reality-warping magical might, they should be someone with very limited magical skill won at great cost, every ritual and spell a great effort. If you want to be someone who can light people on fire or move stuff with your mind, be a psychic. Out of control espers are much more of a horror thing that mages. That's why I'm so excited for Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically what you want to play is an adept from Unknown Armies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T10:20:21-07:00","id":933962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933948#post933948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that Mages in ChroD resemble Potter and Dresden much more than they resemble the examples of monsters that you gave. Also, Hansel and Gretel is Changeling's turf.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, there's no exclusive territory on inspirations. Castlevania's Dracula can be both a Vampire and a Beast, as an example. Gamelines can share sources.<br /> <br /> Second, Has anyone here read Backup, Aftermath, Even Hand, or Bombshells?I've read the first three, and I'm running on assumptions based on that with the fourth.<br /> <br /> No one other than Dresden himself treats Dresden as just a person, a friend. His brother, his love, his enemy, his apprentice-they all speak of Dresden with a measure of dread. Sure, they know where he's benign-but they speak with horror of when Dresden lets loose, or even just how god-fucking creepy as shit it is when Dresden just draws answers from seemingly nowhere. People who have soulgazed him have consistently described him as terrifying.<br /> <br /> Since we read from Dresden's point of view, he's often humanized to us, but to outside perspectives, the man is this kinetic, inexorable force, a laughing, snide madman who flips off gods and demons and <i>wins</i> against them, with hands of wind and fire, haunted eyes that don't see you so much as take you all in-a tower, tall and dark, filled with secrets and schemes.<br /> <br /> So even Dresden's not outside of the sphere.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, Surely I can't say the same about Potter? Surely not. And yeah, maybe not by many of his peers or mentors standards-and yet, while it might cross over into Beast's territory of Hero-dread, consider Voldemort's position.<br /> <br /> Here is a child-a young man at best, perhaps, ultimately a child-marked by the hand of fate, a child who inexorably lives, this feigning, ill-begotten mark in the scheme of destiny, whose hands always burn, who's tools bind the mightiest wizard of an era down, who dives into danger after danger and emerges victorious again and again. He seems to wield, with utter innocence, this strange and impossible force, which he cannot beat time and time again regardless of how utterly simple and juvenille and sentimental it is. This Potter child bound in magics, forces, truths that the Dark Lord cannot comprehend, and they, to the bidding of the child, seem hell bent on destroying him.<br /> <br /> Voldemort blames everyone-<i>anyone</i>-he can for this-Dumbledore, the Potters, Grindelwald, Sirius Black, Death-whoever he can-because he's looking for a way to <i>win</i>, and he knows, as great as some of his foes might be, they operate on laws and logic he can understand. He can <i>beat</i> what he <i>knows</i>. Strip this child of all his support, and surely the terrifying forces at his beck and call will fade. And as Voldemort does just that, his fear <i>grows</i>, because this child, this young man, this <i>occultist</i> knows something he does not, and survives time and time again, an inexorable sun to end his dark night.<br /> <br /> And as for Harry's perspective, one need look no further than the moments when Dumbldore cuts lose, or how he views Voldemort himself-The minimum is awe, the greatest is terror.<br /> <br /> Yes, Potter and Dresden do a lot to mollify wizards, and like those narratives, people are too keen to look from the mage's point of view to see themselves, to be blinded by a certain point of view and fail to see-<br /> <br /> <i>These witches and wizards twitch and the universe responds and they don't even seem to know how far their actions carry, how terrifying they are in their self-innocence.</i><br /> <br /> Even if Dresden were the strongest source for Mage(and it's not, Hellblazer's genes are much stronger), That would still clearly qualify them for their place in the pantheon of modern pulp horror. The fact that the most ardent and vocal fans for Mage often fail to see that just reinforces that there is nothing so terrifying as a powerful figure with little self-awareness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-19-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T10:26:21-07:00","id":933965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933912#post933912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was also a guy named Michael... You're not from Washington state, are you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, no. There are people in Britain too who thought Charmed was a documentary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T10:47:10-07:00","id":933973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933965#post933965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, no. There are people in Britain too who thought Charmed was a documentary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems a disturbingly common misconception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T10:50:08-07:00","id":933974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933965#post933965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, no. There are people in Britain too who thought Charmed was a documentary.</div> </div> </div> </div>and this is the true horror story","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:07:51-07:00","id":934008,"title":"","content":"I won't say brand wasn't a thing, but look at the next game: Promethean. What the hell is a Promethean ? In which horror story did we see a Promethean ? Why not simply call this game Frankenstein ?<br /> Because Promethean is not a game only about Frankenstein monsters. And Mage is not only about Witches. So they choose a more generic, multi-cultural -gendered -whatever term for people who work magic. Which was already the goal in cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T19:12:08-07:00","id":934237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933962#post933962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, there's no exclusive territory on inspirations. Castlevania's Dracula can be both a Vampire and a Beast, as an example. Gamelines can share sources.<br /> <br /> Second, Has anyone here read Backup, Aftermath, Even Hand, or Bombshells?I've read the first three, and I'm running on assumptions based on that with the fourth.<br /> <br /> No one other than Dresden himself treats Dresden as just a person, a friend. His brother, his love, his enemy, his apprentice-they all speak of Dresden with a measure of dread. Sure, they know where he's benign-but they speak with horror of when Dresden lets loose, or even just how god-fucking creepy as shit it is when Dresden just draws answers from seemingly nowhere. People who have soulgazed him have consistently described him as terrifying.<br /> <br /> Since we read from Dresden's point of view, he's often humanized to us, but to outside perspectives, the man is this kinetic, inexorable force, a laughing, snide madman who flips off gods and demons and <i>wins</i> against them, with hands of wind and fire, haunted eyes that don't see you so much as take you all in-a tower, tall and dark, filled with secrets and schemes.<br /> <br /> So even Dresden's not outside of the sphere.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, Surely I can't say the same about Potter? Surely not. And yeah, maybe not by many of his peers or mentors standards-and yet, while it might cross over into Beast's territory of Hero-dread, consider Voldemort's position.<br /> <br /> Here is a child-a young man at best, perhaps, ultimately a child-marked by the hand of fate, a child who inexorably lives, this feigning, ill-begotten mark in the scheme of destiny, whose hands always burn, who's tools bind the mightiest wizard of an era down, who dives into danger after danger and emerges victorious again and again. He seems to wield, with utter innocence, this strange and impossible force, which he cannot beat time and time again regardless of how utterly simple and juvenille and sentimental it is. This Potter child bound in magics, forces, truths that the Dark Lord cannot comprehend, and they, to the bidding of the child, seem hell bent on destroying him.<br /> <br /> Voldemort blames everyone-<i>anyone</i>-he can for this-Dumbledore, the Potters, Grindelwald, Sirius Black, Death-whoever he can-because he's looking for a way to <i>win</i>, and he knows, as great as some of his foes might be, they operate on laws and logic he can understand. He can <i>beat</i> what he <i>knows</i>. Strip this child of all his support, and surely the terrifying forces at his beck and call will fade. And as Voldemort does just that, his fear <i>grows</i>, because this child, this young man, this <i>occultist</i> knows something he does not, and survives time and time again, an inexorable sun to end his dark night.<br /> <br /> And as for Harry's perspective, one need look no further than the moments when Dumbldore cuts lose, or how he views Voldemort himself-The minimum is awe, the greatest is terror.<br /> <br /> Yes, Potter and Dresden do a lot to mollify wizards, and like those narratives, people are too keen to look from the mage's point of view to see themselves, to be blinded by a certain point of view and fail to see-<br /> <br /> <i>These witches and wizards twitch and the universe responds and they don't even seem to know how far their actions carry, how terrifying they are in their self-innocence.</i><br /> <br /> Even if Dresden were the strongest source for Mage(and it's not, Hellblazer's genes are much stronger), That would still clearly qualify them for their place in the pantheon of modern pulp horror. The fact that the most ardent and vocal fans for Mage often fail to see that just reinforces that there is nothing so terrifying as a powerful figure with little self-awareness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent post. I would also add, as far as more obscure stuff goes, Peter Straub's Shadowlands novel as an excellent example of horror genre about people that practice magical traditions. What always surprises me the most I think when people attempt to bring up somewhat lighter aspects of magical people pop culture is that it almost always misses the point that well....people being able to manipulate reality is inherently horrific in and of itself. Obviously that falls at one end of a pretty wide spectrum, but it's as inherent to the idea as the idea of miraculous uses of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:51:33-07:00","id":934289,"title":"","content":"I think they were trying to get the Ascension crowd. The big three were all pretty clearly made full of attempts to get as far as possible away from the World of Darkness versions of the game while still keeping core elements.<br /> <br /> I really wish there was a Witchcraft source book, or some sort of blue book devoted to the occult and various beliefs that the common mortal can understand, or at least confront. The books are full of little pieces of fiction about random mortals who are somehow doing city-threatening things after stumbling upon an occult secret or forgotten lore but there's very little back-up for it in the books, and what there is is scattered across them and clearly not made with each other in mind, like the cults in Second Sight and the witches in Witch Finders.<br /> <br /> The structure for it is all there. There's cults, sorceries and rituals that are accessible to 'lesser' templates. There's been an Occult skill since the origin of the game but for the most part it's there to identify things. And the simple fact that Awakening is so clearly defined and set in its way gives you a lot of room to do other things that wouldn't infringe upon it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-20-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:57:18-07:00","id":934292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=934008#post934008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't say brand wasn't a thing, but look at the next game: Promethean. What the hell is a Promethean ? In which horror story did we see a Promethean ? Why not simply call this game Frankenstein ?<br /> Because Promethean is not a game only about Frankenstein monsters. And Mage is not only about Witches. So they choose a more generic, multi-cultural -gendered -whatever term for people who work magic. Which was already the goal in cWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weeeeell, Frankenstein's subtitle/alt title is &quot;The Modern Prometheus&quot;. The original text deliberately calls on the Prometheus legend. And since, if we're being strictly accurate, &quot;Frankenstein&quot; is the name of the creator and not the created, &quot;Promethean&quot; actually seems more natural a name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T22:55:31-07:00","id":934307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=934292#post934292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weeeeell, Frankenstein's subtitle/alt title is &quot;The Modern Prometheus&quot;. The original text deliberately calls on the Prometheus legend. And since, if we're being strictly accurate, &quot;Frankenstein&quot; is the name of the creator and not the created, &quot;Promethean&quot; actually seems more natural a name.</div> </div> </div> </div>The creature people usually refer to as &quot;Frankenstein&quot; considered himself to be <i>Doctor</i> Frankenstein's son in many ways. While, strictly speaking, his name wasn't &quot;Frankenstein&quot;, he had nearly as much right to the name as a flesh-and-blood son, and if memory serves, he himself held that opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T22:59:57-07:00","id":934308,"title":"","content":"And they <i>did</i> directly reference Frankenstein in the game: that's the name of one of the original five Lineages. But we're not really disagreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3648_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3648\" data-vbnamecard=\"3648\">Nepher</a> here; in fact, his whole point was that \u201cFrankenstein\u201d would have been too specific a name for the game. It would be like calling VtR \u201cDracula\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T23:14:07-07:00","id":934309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933590#post933590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you mention that, I do remember typing 'Karotechia' (a Nazi cthulhu-mythos conspiracy) into google and immediately coming across a 'germanic heritage' forum where the members were discussing it as real history.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the funniest fucking thing I've ever neard<br /> <br /> They're all dead in the new edition of Delta Green, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T23:28:26-07:00","id":934311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=934307#post934307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The creature people usually refer to as &quot;Frankenstein&quot; considered himself to be <i>Doctor</i> Frankenstein's son in many ways. While, strictly speaking, his name wasn't &quot;Frankenstein&quot;, he had nearly as much right to the name as a flesh-and-blood son, and if memory serves, he himself held that opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's reaching a bit though. The creature never refers to himself by that name in the course of the story. Neither does anyone else.<br /> <br /> But my point wasn't about why Promethean <i>isn't</i> called Frankenstein and more about why it is <i>is</i> called Promethean. Because both names derive from the same source and I can make an easier argument for Promethean than Frankenstein (Frankensteinian?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T23:37:24-07:00","id":934316,"title":"","content":"Fun bit of trivia: <b>Promethean: the Created</b> wasn't the first time that White Wolf referred to a Frankenstein's Monster as a \u201cPromethean\u201d. The first time was <i>The Promethean Plague</i>, a 19<sup>th</sup> century <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> setting outlined in the <b>Mage Storyteller's Handbook</b> Revised Edition. I <i>don't</i> think that's a coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T09:54:17-07:00","id":934548,"title":"","content":"Also, on topic of Witches - I want to remember we HAVE them as name. Name of 1/5 of Awakened that follow Acanthus Path. And it does have sense they are only those called that way, like Warlocks are Mastigos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T21:39:12-07:00","id":939333,"title":"","content":"Yeah there are a number of self-identified Witches I have or am gaming with, from Wiccans to Occultists and much in between. They would, I suspect, find a game named witch hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:13:23-07:00","id":942360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches?p=933642#post933642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idunno; C.J. Carella's <b>Witchcraft</b> did reasonably well, and if there's a vocal opposition to it in the Wiccan community, I'm unaware of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the existence of the <b>Witchcraft</b> game has a lot to do with why they stuck with &quot;Mage&quot; (well, that, and brand continuity). I don't know about newer editions, but the original (and the <i>Armageddon</i> spinoff) read a <i>lot</i> like a World of Darkness game. The apocalypse is coming, the Craft is dying, dark creatures stalk the cities . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}